> Interpretability studies what happens inside models.
--- begin text 101112 (wiki, v1.6.0, edited 2025-03-01; written by forum users) ---
# Overview
Interpretability is the study of how models compute.

# Methods
Circuits analysis traces features through layers.

Superposition lets a model store more features than dimensions.

# Open problems
Scaling these methods is hard.
